# What tests/python.rs runs the Python sekisho generates with: cedarpy, the Cedar the generated
# module asks in its own process (`--authorizer cedar`); boto3, which the code of
# `--authorizer avp` calls Verified Permissions with, and its stubs, so that mypy reads that code
# too; and mypy, which holds the generated module to `--strict`. The tests never call AWS.
# requirements.txt is the lock, made from this with
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --python-version 3.13 --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt
# and installed with
#   uv venv --python 3.13 tools/runner-py/.venv
#   uv pip sync --python tools/runner-py/.venv/bin/python --require-hashes tools/runner-py/requirements.txt
#
# The versions are the ones `ritsu gen` writes into a package's pyproject.toml (cedarpy, boto3);
# boto3 is the one dandori's tools/wire holds.
cedarpy==4.12.1
boto3==1.43.103
boto3-stubs[verifiedpermissions]==1.43.103
mypy==2.4.0
